pkg:Evidence_v1_6_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.6.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: user directly challenged whether 1 Area/1 Goal/1 Objective/1 Epic was actually mature, given G29's own closure test names 8 required goals (mission x3 clauses, scope x1, containment x1, exclusion x3) where this lineage had 1. Confirmed real. Applied G28 first (scope derived by testing the Mission against an external taxonomy's structure, not paraphrase): built a reference table from the RDODI Four-Stage Pipeline Procedure v1.3.0's real 4-stage structure crossed against the 3 mission clauses, found the single existing Area (Stage 4 only) badly under-covered Clause 1 ('gate-verifiable at every RDODI stage', which the existing Deliverable already named all 4 stages for) -- split into 3 Areas matching each clause's actual footprint, re-pointed all 3 Deliverables to their correct area, and widened the one scope-facing Goal to cover all 3 areas per G29's exact wording (one goal covering EVERY area, not one goal per area). Then built the G29 completeness layer scoped to this session (containment + exclusion, mission-facing deferred as its own pass): 1 containment-facing Goal+Objective (verified 0 out-of-area work items by direct query) and 3 exclusion-facing Goals+Objectives, each with a real, checked baseline (e.g. 0 commits touching rdodi-ecosystem/ from this session, verified via git log against the actual clone). Adding this content to already-closed stages was correctly caught by backlog_pipeline_verify_v1_0_0.py (3 stage digests failed to reproduce) -- re-closed Stage_Goal/Objective/Backlog with recomputed digests reflecting the real new state, all three genuinely closing together in one commit, disclosed as such (not presented as separately ordered), with closedAtCommit backfilled in a follow-up commit per the framework's own established pending-commit precedent. Re-verified after every step: pipeline order (5/5 digests reproduce), full SHACL at L2 (0 violations). G29 test re-run directly against the final register: 5 of 8 required goals now present and correctly typed (scope-facing 1/1, containment-facing 1/1, exclusion-facing 3/3); mission-facing (3/3) remains open, explicitly deferred with the user's agreement."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "84156281329bfaa918a5ed8d2d954e9146a3b94d23fb3ecb29977fa798ea5afe"^^xsd:string .
